{"skill":{"slug":"transcript","displayName":"transcript"},"version":{"version":"1.5.1","createdAt":1789981691830,"changelog":"Expanded endpoint coverage: video metadata, channel info/playlists/posts/sections, search filters, format tabs (uploads/Shorts/streams)","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4444,"sha256":"942815adbde443a4e9dc0310304ef7dcc9c4623eca9b3ce86ba933a99e3eb099","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/auth-setup.md","size":7373,"sha256":"9b883d30ad32beedd443d2aef9d56f42f9aef7b30dd67e7c6f104d1bcc70319f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2152,"sha256":"77f2f4cc834ec7164175fc6dbad076baba027f88dc558a826d6373baf153e2d9","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789982695041,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7092f36fc5f45100f31ad009f8f477cc47a82e0f078e75511d7462ca2e111b0c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7092f36fc5f45100f31ad009f8f477cc47a82e0f078e75511d7462ca2e111b0c","scanners":{"vt":null,"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789982695041},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This transcript skill does what it says, but its setup flow gives the agent broad, persistent control over API credentials and account signup.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to TranscriptAPI is expected, but the skill does not clearly foreground that YouTube URLs or IDs, authorization headers, user-agent details, and account signup email may be sent to the third-party service.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is markdown-only with no executable installer or bundled code, but setup instructions tell the agent to modify persistent environment configuration for future sessions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill tells agents to use it even when transcript retrieval is not explicitly requested for broad video-based tasks, which can trigger third-party transcript requests beyond clear user intent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The setup guide explicitly instructs persistent storage of TRANSCRIPT_API_KEY across future sessions and describes file-based handling of raw auth responses to avoid redacted tool output.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Transcript retrieval through TranscriptAPI is coherent with the stated purpose, but the referenced setup guide expands into agent-led third-party account creation, OTP handling, API key extraction, and durable credential setup.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review carefully before installing. Use this skill only if you are comfortable sending video identifiers and account-related data to TranscriptAPI. Prefer creating the account yourself and entering the API key through a dedicated secret manager rather than pasting it into chat or letting the agent persist it broadly across sessions.","findings":"[SSD-3] unexpected: The artifact does ask users to paste an API key into chat and instructs file-based extraction of access tokens and API keys; credential use is needed for the service, but this handling and persistence are higher-risk than necessary.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The artifact supports agent-led account registration and OTP verification, which is setup-related but materially broader than simple transcript retrieval.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The artifact directs the agent to make the API key available in future sessions, including non-interactive shells, creating durable access without sufficiently scoped retention controls.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The activation text says to use the skill for video-source research and summarization even when transcript retrieval is not explicitly requested, increasing the chance of unnecessary third-party calls.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact discloses use of TranscriptAPI, but does not provide clear consent language before persistent secret storage, email-based signup, or transmission of request data to the provider.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The static SARIF scan reported no T01-T09 results; my Review verdict is based on the markdown setup instructions, not on a static malicious-code finding.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789982695041}}}}}